From c61e90c9cdfb466336d3f564a1a3709f3daecc65 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Diego Amicabile <diego.amicabile@soprasteria.com>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 17:27:55 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Borg: return the best Maim Foe score from the real call

borg_attack_aux_maim_foe()'s real path saved the best target (b_i/b_d),
aimed at it, and then returned d -- the score of the last monster the
loop examined -- instead of b_d. With two adjacent monsters where the
best one is examined first, the function reported the worse monster's
score; the trailing 'if (borg_simulate) return d;' behind it was dead
(the simulation path already returned b_d). Return b_d.
---
 src/borg/borg-fight-attack.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/borg/borg-fight-attack.c b/src/borg/borg-fight-attack.c
index 62136e297..cd2ca0c02 100644
--- a/src/borg/borg-fight-attack.c
+++ b/src/borg/borg-fight-attack.c
@@ -3498,7 +3498,7 @@ static int borg_attack_aux_maim_foe(void)
     borg_spell(MAIM_FOE);
     borg_keypress(I2D(dir));
 
-    return d;
+    return b_d;
 }
 
 /* trying the Vampire Strike spell */
